 on this jacket? This one, because it's a full zip, a lot of times, like the old Nano Air was a pullover. And that's all they offered it in. And so I bought one. I bought my normal size large. And I have a little bit of a trouble with that half zip stuff. I mean, anyways, I ended up having to upsize on that Nano Air to an XL. But this one I ordered is a large. It's a full zip. And it fits perfect. It's slightly athletic, but fairly close to regular fit. Yeah, so pretty standard sizing there. And I did see that one of the things you mentioned is using this with a wind shirt and you get this insulation piece. You can really be super active, but still have the warmth and block some air. Like, let's say, if you were snowshoeing and it wasn't super cold. Yep, absolutely. Yeah, this piece combined with a light wind shirt would get you through a lot of different weather. With this jacket, it has a DWR. And I've had it out in some pretty light, especially like snow. It does a really good job. You know, if you start spitting rain, you know, the DWR is going to get overwhelmed eventually. And it's going to win out. A wind shirt usually offers a little bit better DWR. So you put that over it. I mean, you're blocking more wind. You're holding more heat in. But you're still able to vent and breathe moisture from your body out and stuff. It's kind of a killer combo for not a lot of weight. All right, buddy. I'll get your link up to your review there. And if people get any questions, they can reach out to you there on Rockslide. Absolutely. All right, Mike. I appreciate it there. No problem, Sam. Okay, Rocksliders. Robbie Denning here. I wanted to get Stephen Lathrop on the Rockcast today. He's been on with Sam a few times. I've worked with him for well over a decade. And I went to their wide boot fit earlier this spring. And we're going to talk about that and why I went to it. And I can just tell you this. If you look down at your feet and you look like Shrek, you really need to 